  ],
  "q4_value": "sense_blast retained_via_interfaces surfaced the exact class of holder the ticket was about — subsystems retaining the server behind a small local interface (Planner/JobEvalDispatcher/RaftApplier/Encrypter/CSIVolumeRPC) that never name or import nomad.Server — complete with the carrier→Server chain AND a via_satisfiers signal that let me separate genuine in-process retainers from the client-side RPCer false positives; grep could never have assembled that interface-satisfaction graph in one call.",
  "q5_improve": "For each retained_via_interfaces row, include the field's assignment/construction site (where the concrete carrier is injected), not just the field declaration — I had to Read server.go and the setup* funcs to recover those handoff lines for Steps 3 and 5.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "The retained_via_interfaces graph and dispatch-inferred satisfier chains (Q1 accurate) gave me the interface-typed holders with their carrier→Server paths that no grep could reconstruct, and the only fallbacks (Q2) were for method-body content Sense deliberately omits, not for locations it failed to provide."
}

